You want to start a business then learn about what it means to run a business first You do not need a degree but a course or two will definitely help. Basic accounting and a little law will save you in the long run. You do not need to keep the books just understand them.

Rule one: Incorporate - protects you from partners liabilities and insulates you from unsecured creditors;
Rule two: Bookkeeper - hire one if you can't do Quickbooks;
Rule three: Accountant - get one for tax and financial advise;
Rule four: pay your statutory creditors first and on time or they will ruin you;
Rule five: always review what your partner is doing and vice versa. If they keep the books review them.

In this case your operations had to be losing money and the conversation between partners should have been "do we get financing". In this case Mr. Dawson may not have been able to do so given his debt so he chose the fools option use the HST. Count yourself lucky he did not use the payroll remittance as well.

